<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/General-iCloud-App-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Yesterday we reported that Apple tripled the number of iCloud Mail aliases users can create, from <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/05/apple-triples-icloud-mail-alias-limit/">three to nine</a>. But it turns out that's not the only email-related limit Apple has raised. The company has also bumped the number of iCloud Custom Domains users can set up with iCloud+, from three to 10.<br/>
